  "id": "formal-discipline",
  "term": "formal discipline",
  "definition": "Formal discipline is the idea that studying a demanding subject, especially mathematics, strengthens general thinking or logical reasoning skills beyond that subject itself. In this context, the theory is discussed as a claim about whether learning mathematics transfers to broader reasoning ability.",
